   "name": "Types of food nutrients; macronutrients"
  }
 ],
 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Nutrients are the substances in food that the body needs to live, grow and stay healthy. There are six classes:\ncarbohydrates, proteins, fats (lipids), vitamins, minerals and water. (Fibre is also needed, though it is not digested.)\n• Macronutrients are needed in large amounts (grams each day): carbohydrates, proteins and fats. They give energy and build the body.\n• Micronutrients are needed in small amounts (milligrams or micrograms): vitamins and minerals. They protect the body and control its work.\nMost foods contain several nutrients, but one usually stands out: rice and cassava are mainly carbohydrate; fish and beans are rich in protein; palm oil is fat.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "m": "rice, fish stew and an orange"
  },
  "problem": "Name the main nutrient in each part of a meal of {m}.",
  "steps": [
   "Rice: mainly carbohydrate (starch).",
   "Fish: mainly protein; the oil in the stew: fat.",
   "Orange: vitamin C and water."
  ],
  "answer": "Rice: carbohydrate; fish: protein; oil: fat; orange: vitamin C and water.",
  "checks": []
 },
